  "findings": [
    "Observed failure was an 8-second servo-data GATT read timeout followed by the Web bridge disconnecting. UART reported TX pool exhaustion before the failure.",
    "Servo interpolation calls the characteristic update on changes, normally at up to 50 Hz plus wakeups. The update also sends notifications when subscribed.",
    "The servo-data read handler invokes that same notifying update before permitting the read, coupling a control read to available notification TX resources.",
    "Repeat restart reads servo values in holdActiveTimedMoves, then enqueueServoDcUpdates reads them again, followed by another read for the next initial snapshot.",
    "The disabled-notification comparison passed 191.248 seconds; re-enabling notifications then also passed 177.718 seconds. Notification pressure is a supported investigation direction, not a uniquely proven deterministic root cause.",
    "The current firmware logged disconnection and resumed advertising; the captured CPU was idle with no fault flags. A permanent MCU hard lock was not demonstrated.",
    "Reconnection was attempted after debugger halting and failed to discover the board until reset. Debugger timing perturbed radio operation, so this does not independently reproduce the original inability to reconnect.",
    "Queue enqueue failure paths leak allocated payloads, but the captured queues were empty and the baseline UART contained 241 successful TX replies for 241 NUS writes; this run did not establish that leak as the cause."
  ],
  "recommended_next_changes": [
    "Separate servo characteristic database refresh from notification emission; use the no-notify update path during reads and acknowledge reads independently of telemetry TX pool capacity.",
    "Coalesce/rate-limit servo telemetry and handle BUSY/INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES with bounded retry when TX capacity returns.",
    "Remove redundant snapshot reads during repeat restarts, preserving atomic channel updates.",
    "Fix RX/TX enqueue-failure memory ownership and add queue/resource counters separately.",
    "Add retained crash/reset diagnostics and a designed watchdog recovery path; do not infer a hard fault from the UI cursor alone."
  ],
